  "query_preview": "..\nToday through Next Thursday: An upper ridge will dominate the\nwestern US providing dry conditions and above normal\ntemperatures through the middle of next week. Occasionally the\nridge will be flattened by mid level waves passing through\nbringing passing mid and high clouds. One such wave will pass\nthrough on Friday. Then the ridge strengthens leading to mostly\nclear skies Saturday through Monday. This will also bring the\nwarmest temperatures of the 7 day forecast with highs in the 70s\nto low 80s. Then towards the middle of next week additional \nwaves pass through for more mid and high clouds and high\ntemperatures falling into the upper 60s to mid 70s. Night time\nlows with the longer nights and dry air will vary depending on\nlocation with the warmest spots such as Wenatchee and Lewiston\nas warm as the low to mid 50s, while areas with stronger \nradiational cooling such as the northern valleys drop into the \nmid 30s to low 40s. JW",
